[00:06:56] Ozan Er: What if it just says there's no debt because no statement has been cut yet, and then, if the answer has it, when the first one comes. Only that date, exactly as the service gives it. Nothing else.\n[00:07:07] Ozan Er: Something like \"Kartınızın henüz kesilmiş bir ekstresi olmadığı için ekstre borcunuz bulunmamaktadır. İlk hesap kesim tarihiniz 5 Kasım 2026 olacak.\" with the date from the answer.\n[00:07:17] Kerem Yalçın: Yeah, let's do that.\n[00:07:19] Selin Aydın: Mm.\n[00:07:20] Kerem Yalçın: And if there's no date in the answer either, it just says there's no debt. That's fine too. Just nothing made up.\n[00:07:25] Deniz Arı: Is somebody frying something?\n[00:07:27] Burcu Tan: [laughs] That's my kitchen. Muting.\n[00:07:30] Selin Aydın: Ozan, how many more? Kerem has to go.\n[00:07:33] Ozan Er: Not a call, a dry run. Deniz played the customer.\n[00:07:36] Deniz Arı: The cut day. We can't hit it with the test data, the dates are fixed, so I told the assistant today is the cut day and called.\n[00:07:44] Ozan Er: [plays recording, about fifteen seconds]\n[00:07:59] Burcu Tan: It started with the due date.\n[00:08:01] Ozan Er: Yes. \"Borçlarınız için son ödeme tarihiniz [son ödeme tarihi]'dir.\" first, then the amount.\n[00:08:07] Burcu Tan: In the IVR the first thing is that the statement is cut tonight. \"Hesap kesim tarihiniz bugün, ekstreniz saat 00.00 itibarıyla kesilecek.\" That's in Selin's document too, it's what the menu does today.\n[00:08:17] Deniz Arı: And then after that the normal reading, the statement debt, like any other day?\n[00:08:21] Kerem Yalçın: I don't mind how it opens, honestly.\n[00:08:23] Burcu Tan: I do, a bit. People hear the due date and think the bill is out.\n[00:08:27] Kerem Yalçın: Fine, then use yours. But the other one isn't wrong. What I care about is the number.\n[00:08:32] Selin Aydın: Which number did it read, Ozan?\n[00:08:34] Ozan Er: The statement debt. From the last statement.\n[00:08:37] Kerem Yalçın: That's the problem then. On the cut day the last statement is from a month ago. They need the total, with everything they spent since then in it.\n[00:08:44] Deniz Arı: Ah, so not what I said. Not the normal reading.\n[00:08:46] Kerem Yalçın: No. Opening whichever, then the total debt.\n[00:08:49] Ozan Er: The totalDebt field then, per currency. Mert's contract says it includes the spending after the statement.\n[00:08:55] Selin Aydın: Yes, that one.\n[00:08:57] Burcu Tan: I'd still put the 00.00 one first. It tells them why the number is bigger than the last bill.\n[00:09:02] Kerem Yalçın: Put it first. I just don't want the other one treated as wrong.\n[00:09:06] Burcu Tan: Okay, okay.\n[00:09:08] Ozan Er: And the currency names in the total too, full names. [laughs] Before Kerem says it.\n[00:09:12] Kerem Yalçın: [laughs] Good.\n[00:09:14] Kerem Yalçın: Guys, I need to drive. Anything else that needs me?\n[00:09:17] Deniz Arı: No, the rest is on our side. The voice speed on long amounts.\n[00:09:20] Kerem Yalçın: Okay. Bye all.\n[00:09:22] Burcu Tan: Bye Kerem, good game.\n[00:09:24] Selin Aydın: Bye.\n[00:09:26] Selin Aydın: Deniz, I won't get to the document this weekend. Can you send Elçin and Mert a few lines?\n[00:09:31] Deniz Arı: Yes, I'll write something short. Maybe Monday morning.\n[00:09:34] Selin Aydın: Monday is fine.\n[00:09:36] Ozan Er: Selin, the mobile app topic from Wednesday, is that still next week?\n[00:09:40] Selin Aydın: Next week, yes, Thursday I think. Kerem sends the invite.\n[00:09:44] Ozan Er: Okay.\n[00:09:45] Burcu Tan: Deniz, send me the recording link too? I want my team to hear the \"ge be pe\" [laughs].\n[00:09:50] Deniz Arı: [laughs] Sure.\n[00:09:52] Burcu Tan: Okay, kids are calling. Bye.\n[00:09:54] Selin Aydın: Bye. Thanks both, enjoy the weekend.\n[00:09:56] Deniz Arı: You too. Bye.\n\n[recording stopped]\n\n\n===== DOCUMENT: final-case-input/statement-debt-call-flow.pdf =====\nCall arrives from IVR\nSupervisor detects